+## What this does
+
+The model's index tool (`link-model-part`) can now take in old parts of the product model once a person approved it. Three steps had no tool, and the #1021 review of Orchestration (BI-9) was blocked on all three: its first capability takes in View plans, Manage a plan and Shape a slice.
+
+- **`thin: false`** takes a capability's or feature's thin mark off both places it lives, the index entry and the page's Thin line, so the part can take a full ICE of its own in the same request.
+- **`capability: <id>`** files a feature under another capability, one in the index or added earlier in the same request. Only a feature takes it.
+- **`doc: <new path>`** moves a page, and the ice.md beside it, to a new folder that a part of its kind may use; the entry's doc and its ICE entry's doc follow, and the old folder is removed. It is refused while any page or record names an old path, while the old folder holds any other file, when the new folder already holds a file, or when another part, or another move in the same request, already uses the new folder.
+- A write that fails part way puts every file and folder back; each undo step is tried on its own, and when one cannot finish the error names every path that is not back.
+- The skill's rules now say a feature with a capability moves only through this update, that a re-file gives `doc` with `capability`, and that the caller records the person's approval. The `product-os-keeper` agent lists the three updates in its table, its boundaries and a mapping row for the order (clear the mark, write the approved pages, then index and move).
+
+## After the review's reject
+
+The reviewer rejected the first raise on R-1: two moves into one folder lost a page. This raise fixes R-1 (refused: two parts never share a folder), R-2 (the undo is best-effort and names what is not back), R-3 (tests for the delete, folder-removal and undo path) and the four harness doc gaps H-L2-1 to H-L2-4. The other findings stay open, as listed in the review's comment.
+
+The acceptance check (`.garura/project/issues/1037/evidence/eval/eval_1037.py`) was committed first, failing (5 of 26), and passes 30 of 30. The skill's unit tests: 48, all passing. The component check reads 36 errors and 1 warning before and after, none in the files changed.
+
+## Raised past a failed self-review check
+
+The pre-push check (`check_self_review.py`) exited 1 on two commit subjects over the 72-character cap: 339ddf54 (156 characters) and 6de7f7c6 (82 characters). The product owner chose to raise past both, recorded in `.garura/project/issues/1037/context/raise-past-check.md`. The long subjects stay in the history, and this run of /propose-change does not close COMPLETED.
+
+Closes #1037
