+# design-findings-harness.yaml: Layer 2 (design-grounding + conformance) for the "harness" category
+# of PR #1038 (issue #1037). Written by change-reviewer, Job 2, one category per dispatch.
+# Every principle below is read from outside the branch: the base ref (main), a decision record
+# committed on another branch, or Phoenix memory read through the memory tool. Nothing is grounded
+# in prose this branch adds. The base ref is main (1be69342).
+pr: 1038
+issue: 1037
+category: harness
+base: main
+artifacts_in_scope:
+  - core/components/skills/link-model-part/SKILL.md
+  - core/components/agents/product-os-keeper.md
+read_as_implementation_only:
+  - core/components/skills/link-model-part/scripts/link_part.py   # its code quality is the executable-code category's
+memory:
+  memory_dir: .garura/project/issues/1037/context/memory/grounding-harness/
+  manifest: .garura/project/issues/1037/context/memory/grounding-harness/manifest.json
+  copied_through_the_memory_tool:
+    - standards/rules/direct-model-write.md
+    - standards/schemas/product-os/ontology.md
+    - standards/schemas/product-os/spine.yaml
+    - standards/rules/naming.md
+    - standards/rules/naming.yaml
+  shared_copies_read: [.garura/project/issues/1037/context/memory/knowledge/review/harness.md, .garura/project/issues/1037/context/memory/standards/rules/pr.md]
+severity_basis: >-
+  Layer 2 findings have no Standard ID row in pr.md (the table is the scan's, and the scan is not
+  eligible on garura-prose). Each finding takes the bucket from the pr.md definitions: P1 blocker
+  (security, secrets, data loss, breaking API contract); P2 major (structural violations); P3 minor
+  (missing docs, borderline, naming); P4 nit (suppressed by default, shown in evidence).
+
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# The principles, each with its committed source
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+principles:
+  - id: G1
+    principle: >-
+      A skill is a contract of file paths; the mechanical work is a script the skill runs; the
+      handoff carries paths, never contents.
+    sources:
+      - {ref: "main:docs/standards/harness-standard.md", where: "principles 2 and 3"}
+      - {ref: "main:docs/philosophy/architecture.md", where: "line 161, 'Every handoff ... is a JSON contract ... paths, never the contents'"}
+  - id: G2
+    principle: "Build the eval first, and run it against today's code, where it must fail."
+    sources:
+      - {ref: "main:docs/standards/harness-standard.md", where: "principle 5"}
+  - id: G3
+    principle: "An installed part reads, runs and names only installed files; no pointer to core/ or docs/; no note of origin."
+    sources:
+      - {ref: "main:docs/standards/harness-standard.md", where: "principle 11"}
+      - {ref: "main:docs/adr/055-installed-parts-read-only-installed-files.md"}
+  - id: G4
+    principle: "One name, one meaning: each verb in a part's name holds one meaning."
+    sources:
+      - {ref: "main:docs/standards/harness-standard.md", where: "principle 10"}
+      - {ref: "memory tool: phoenix standards/rules/naming.yaml (b2e40bff2131)", where: "verb `link`: 'Make links in the model.'"}
+  - id: G5
+    principle: >-
+      Who may write the model's index (the spine). Base ref: only a play's keyed script, plus
+      link-model-gaps inside a loop. Decided later (ADR 065, rule 1): two skills change the index.
+      link-model-part adds or changes a part; remove-model-part takes a part out, with the name of
+      the person who approved it. Each changes only what its request names, stays inside the
+      model, and lists every file it changed.
+    sources:
+      - {ref: "main:docs/adr/026-direct-to-model-writes.md", where: "Decision, 'Containment split'"}
+      - {ref: "memory tool: phoenix standards/rules/direct-model-write.md (b2e40bff2131)", where: "rule 3 and its 'Inside a loop (ADR 044)' paragraph"}
+      - ref: "feature/1021-reorganise-business-intents:docs/adr/065-the-models-index-is-changed-through-two-skills-the-model-never-names-a-plan-and-only-tools-know-the-tracker.md (commit d6ccf160)"
+        where: "Decision, rule 1"
+        status: "Accepted (2026-11-02) but NOT on the base ref. It is committed outside this branch, and the branch does not add it. See grounding_caveats."
+  - id: G6
+    principle: >-
+      A skill whose act waits for a person's approval takes the person's name in its request and
+      refuses a request without it. The name is a field, so the approval leaves a trace.
+    sources:
+      - {ref: "main:core/components/skills/remove-model-part/SKILL.md", where: "Input (`approved_by`) and Rules, 'Never without the person's name. A request with no approved_by is refused.'"}
+      - {ref: "main:core/components/skills/enrich-grounding/SKILL.md", where: "line 31, `approved_request`: `approved_by` and `source` (where the approval is recorded)"}
+      - {ref: "main:core/components/skills/author-intent-page/SKILL.md", where: "line 25, `confirmed_by`"}
+      - {ref: "feature/1021 ADR 065 (d6ccf160)", where: "rule 1, removal 'with the name of the person who approved it'"}
+  - id: G7
+    principle: >-
+      A mechanical index skill writes no page words. Where a change would leave a line on a page
+      naming something that no longer holds, it refuses and names the line; the page skill changes
+      the words first.
+    sources:
+      - {ref: "main:core/components/skills/link-model-part/SKILL.md", where: "Rules, 'No page words' (base version)"}
+      - {ref: "main:core/components/skills/remove-model-part/SKILL.md", where: "Rules, 'No page words'"}
+  - id: G8
+    principle: >-
+      The product ontology: a feature has exactly one parent capability, and its page lives under
+      its capability's folder (or the holding folder until it names one); its business intents are
+      the ones its parent capability serves; an ICE lives on its own page `ice.md` in its part's
+      folder, so it moves with its part; the thin mark is kept in two places that agree and is
+      removed by the play that deepens the part; rules never stop a write, and drift is found and
+      fixed by the Alignment loop.
+    sources:
+      - {ref: "memory tool: phoenix standards/schemas/product-os/ontology.md (b2e40bff2131)", where: "Feature (Lives at; Relationships; Rules), ICE (Lives at; Thin mark), 'Who writes, and what the rules mean'"}
+      - {ref: "memory tool: phoenix standards/schemas/product-os/spine.yaml (b2e40bff2131)", where: "features block; `thin` comment 'the play that deepens it removes it'"}
+      - {ref: "main:core/grounding/glossary.md", where: "line 63, Feature: 'a feature has one parent capability'"}
+  - id: G9
+    principle: >-
+      The sibling that already re-parents a loose node moves its page under the new parent's
+      folder and lets the spine `doc` follow, in one act. A node already under another parent is
+      skipped there as alignment work.
+    sources:
+      - {ref: "main:core/components/skills/link-model-gaps/SKILL.md", where: "Process 1 and 2 ('a page in a holding folder moves ... under its parent's folder'; 'a node already under another parent - moving it is alignment work')"}
+  - id: G10
+    principle: >-
+      When link-model-part gains a use, the keeper agent's three statements of it move together:
+      its skill-table row, its Intent-to-Skill mapping row, and its Boundaries bullet on who writes
+      the spine. This is the keeper's own committed practice.
+    sources:
+      - {ref: "main:core/components/agents/product-os-keeper.md", where: "Boundaries bullet 'Change the product model by hand' and the mapping row 'write these pages as the person approved them'"}
+      - {ref: "main git history of that file", where: "5497c9c3 (#1031) added the table row and the mapping row; aa3a5d2f (#1031) extended the Boundaries bullet with 'or an ICE's entry (#1031)'"}
+  - id: G11
+    principle: "When no skill covers a change, say so and stop: the missing skill is built, never worked around."
+    sources:
+      - {ref: "main:core/components/agents/product-os-keeper.md", where: "Boundaries, NEVER, 'Change the product model by hand'"}
+  - id: G12
+    principle: "A SKILL.md `description` is a short summary for tooling discovery."
+    sources:
+      - {ref: "main:docs/components/skills.md", where: "SKILL.md Frontmatter table, `description`"}
