+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# Where the change conforms (no finding)
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+conforms:
+  - {principle: G1, evidence: "SKILL.md Input takes only paths (`request`, `product_base`, `out`) and Output returns a report path; the three updates are done by `scripts/link_part.py`, with no judgment in the skill. allowed-tools stays Read, Bash."}
+  - {principle: G2, evidence: "git log main..HEAD: 339ddf54 (the acceptance check, eval_1037.py, alone in that commit) comes before 019f1baa (the feature). The PR body says it failed 5 of 26 first; the tests category runs it."}
+  - {principle: G3, evidence: "The added lines of SKILL.md and product-os-keeper.md hold no core/, docs/ or .garura/core path and no note of origin (grep of the diff). lint-components, source layout, run read-only: 36 errors and 1 warning, none in either changed file."}
+  - {principle: G5, evidence: "The three updates stay inside <product_base>product-os/ (`inside()` refuses a path that leaves it), run all or nothing, and list every file changed (`changed` now also holds each deleted old page). This is rule 1 of ADR 065 for 'adds or changes a part'. The conformance holds only once ADR 065 lands; see grounding_caveats."}
+  - {principle: G7, evidence: "A move is refused while any page or record names the old path (names_of); it does not rewrite those lines. Same pattern as remove-model-part."}
+  - {principle: G8, evidence: "`capability` replaces the single parent (never appends) and only a feature takes it; `doc` moves the page and the ice.md beside it and the ICE entry's doc follows; `thin: false` removes both marks together."}
+  - {principle: G11, evidence: "The change builds the missing step as a skill update rather than working around it. #1037 exists because the #1021 review had no tool for these three steps."}
+  - {principle: "harness-standard principle 4", evidence: "No play or loop is in changed_paths, so there is no ICE source to trace and no lint_play run; a skill has no ICE source."}
